		<item>
		<title>Ukrainian assault units liberate Mali Shcherbaky in southern Zaporizhzhia Oblast</title>
		<link>https://euromaidanpress.com/2025/10/12/ukrainian-assault-units-liberate-mala-shcherbaky-in-southern-zaporizhzhia-oblast/</link>
		
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[Yuri Zoria]]></dc:creator>
		<pubDate>Sun, 12 Oct 2025 17:35:46 +0000</pubDate>
				<category><![CDATA[Latest news Ukraine]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[128th Mountain Assault Brigade]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[24th Aidar Battalion]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[33rd Assault Regiment]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Kamianske]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[liberation]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[main]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Mali Shcherbaky]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Pyatykhatky]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Shcherbaky]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Stepove]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Zaporizhzhia Oblast]]></category>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">https://euromaidanpress.com/?p=366176</guid>

					<description><![CDATA[Ukrainian forces didn’t just take back Mala Shcherbaky—they also pushed  into Russian-held territory across a 5-kilometer front.]]></description>
										<content:encoded><![CDATA[<p><img width="1024" height="492" src="https://euromaidanpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/mali-shcherbaky-on-ukraine-map-flag-1024x492.jpg" class="attachment-large size-large wp-post-image" alt="ukrainian assault units liberate mala shcherbaky southern zaporizhzhia oblast · post novi (situation 12 2025 mali-shcherbaky-on-ukraine-map-flag two troops have liberated village mali russian forces outlet militarnyi reports settlement located 16" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="https://euromaidanpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/mali-shcherbaky-on-ukraine-map-flag-1024x492.jpg 1024w, https://euromaidanpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/mali-shcherbaky-on-ukraine-map-flag-300x144.jpg 300w, https://euromaidanpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/mali-shcherbaky-on-ukraine-map-flag-1536x738.jpg 1536w, https://euromaidanpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/mali-shcherbaky-on-ukraine-map-flag-380x183.jpg 380w, https://euromaidanpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/mali-shcherbaky-on-ukraine-map-flag-800x384.jpg 800w, https://euromaidanpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/mali-shcherbaky-on-ukraine-map-flag-1160x557.jpg 1160w, https://euromaidanpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/mali-shcherbaky-on-ukraine-map-flag.jpg 1574w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px" /></p><div data-type="_mgwidget" data-widget-id="1845881"></div>        
        <script>
            (function(w,q){w[q]=w[q]||[];w[q].push(["_mgc.load"])})(window,"_mgq");
        </script>
    
<p></p>


<p>Two units of Ukrainian assault troops have liberated the village of Mali Shcherbaky in Zaporizhzhia Oblast from Russian forces, Ukrainian outlet Militarnyi reports. The settlement is located 16 km east of the drained Kakhovka Reservoir on the Dnipro River, not far from the town of Orikhiv. </p>
<article class="text-token-text-primary w-full focus:outline-none [--shadow-height:45px] has-data-writing-block:pointer-events-none has-data-writing-block:-mt-(--shadow-height) has-data-writing-block:pt-(--shadow-height) [&amp;:has([data-writing-block])&gt;*]:pointer-events-auto scroll-mt-[calc(var(--header-height)+min(200px,max(70px,20svh)))]" dir="auto" tabindex="-1" data-turn-id="request-68e95ca8-5b08-8330-a7af-cb9c7d2d18b1-129" data-testid="conversation-turn-6" data-scroll-anchor="true" data-turn="assistant">
<div class="text-base my-auto mx-auto pb-10 [--thread-content-margin:--spacing(4)] thread-sm:[--thread-content-margin:--spacing(6)] thread-lg:[--thread-content-margin:--spacing(16)] px-(--thread-content-margin)">
<div class="[--thread-content-max-width:40rem] thread-lg:[--thread-content-max-width:48rem] mx-auto max-w-(--thread-content-max-width) flex-1 group/turn-messages focus-visible:outline-hidden relative flex w-full min-w-0 flex-col agent-turn" tabindex="-1">
<div class="flex max-w-full flex-col grow">
<div class="min-h-8 text-message relative flex w-full flex-col items-end gap-2 text-start break-words whitespace-normal [.text-message+&amp;]:mt-1" dir="auto" data-message-author-role="assistant" data-message-id="7e3f4fc7-99bd-4106-bdcc-1fafdbcbd522" data-message-model-slug="gpt-4o">
<div class="flex w-full flex-col gap-1 empty:hidden first:pt-[1px]">
<div class="markdown prose dark:prose-invert w-full break-words light markdown-new-styling pk-content-block pk-block-bg pk-block-bg-light">
<p data-start="0" data-end="335" data-is-last-node="" data-is-only-node="">Mali Shcherbaky, on the frontline since March 2022 when Russian forces first occupied it, was liberated by Ukrainian forces in May 2022, reoccupied by Russian forces in April 2025, partially held in a gray zone soon after, and fully recaptured by Ukrainian forces on 12 October 2025.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</article>
<h3 id="ukrainian-storm-troops-retake-mali-shcherbaky-in-coordinated-push">Ukrainian storm troops retake Mali Shcherbaky in coordinated push</h3><div data-fuse="incontent_1"></div>
<p>Militarnyi <a href="https://militarnyi.com/uk/news/shturmovi-pidrozdily-zvilnyly-selo-mali-shherbaky-zaporizkoyi-oblasti/">says</a> the Ukrainian flag now flies over Mali Shcherbaky after units from the 24th Aidar Battalion and the 33rd Separate Assault Regiment carried out a successful assault in the Zaporizhzhia sector. The press service of the Aidar Battalion <a href="https://t.me/aidar_24/897">confirmed</a> the liberation, stating that the village is now fully under the control of Ukraine’s Defense Forces.</p>
<figure id="attachment_366186" aria-describedby="caption-attachment-366186" style="width: 1335px" class="wp-caption aligncenter"><a href="https://euromaidanpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/mali-shcherbaky-zaporizhzhia-oblast.jpg"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" class="size-full wp-image-366186" src="https://euromaidanpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/mali-shcherbaky-zaporizhzhia-oblast.jpg" alt="insert/edit link immediate area novi shcherbaky zaporizhzhia oblast situation 12 2025 deep state mali ukraine news ukrainian reports" width="1335" height="701" srcset="https://euromaidanpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/mali-shcherbaky-zaporizhzhia-oblast.jpg 1335w, https://euromaidanpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/mali-shcherbaky-zaporizhzhia-oblast-300x158.jpg 300w, https://euromaidanpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/mali-shcherbaky-zaporizhzhia-oblast-1024x538.jpg 1024w, https://euromaidanpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/mali-shcherbaky-zaporizhzhia-oblast-380x200.jpg 380w, https://euromaidanpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/mali-shcherbaky-zaporizhzhia-oblast-800x420.jpg 800w, https://euromaidanpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/mali-shcherbaky-zaporizhzhia-oblast-1160x609.jpg 1160w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 1335px) 100vw, 1335px" /></a><figcaption id="caption-attachment-366186" class="wp-caption-text">The immediate area of Novi Shcherbaky, Zaporizhzhia Oblast. Situation as of 12 October 2025. Map: Deep State.</figcaption></figure>
<p>Valentyn Manko, head of the Ukrainian Armed Forces’ assault troops directorate, <a href="https://www.facebook.com/100004420939335/videos/pcb.3234116390079027/677321085423069?__cft__%5B0%5D=AZV2oEZeSt34LnMnrDeiNVY_9cL6JkSbz_3b05wrbsmd2UyAE1LRZi3BC9BrUZbIRBa268PCOT10qkB1FWw6dxNfBFRAWrr64h8I5nLslmouOAMh4InZaYIcbnrHnjEDLODKyXzsjziTVzt3ysQASPTdoq01ynDSAJrqDGKha9isycCNUEinqBh_PrXHJ3w43os&amp;__tn__=*b0H-R">reported</a> that the success in Mali Shcherbaky was part of a wider advance. <strong>He noted on Facebook that Ukrainian forces also cleared the nearby village of Shcherbaky and partially liberated Stepove, extending their gains across a 5-kilometer-wide section of the front line.</strong></p>
<p>Militarnyi <a href="https://militarnyi.com/uk/news/shturmovi-pidrozdily-zvilnyly-selo-mali-shherbaky-zaporizkoyi-oblasti/">notes</a> that storm units moved 3.5 kilometers forward in their offensive across the five-kilometer span of the frontline, reversing earlier Russian territorial gains.</p>
<figure id="attachment_366194" aria-describedby="caption-attachment-366194" style="width: 1919px" class="wp-caption aligncenter"><a href="https://euromaidanpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/24-oshb-Ajdar-ta-33-OSHP-v-Malyh-shherbakah-12.10.2025.-Stop-kadr-z-video-24-bataljonu-Ajdar-1.png"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" class="size-full wp-image-366194" src="https://euromaidanpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/24-oshb-Ajdar-ta-33-OSHP-v-Malyh-shherbakah-12.10.2025.-Stop-kadr-z-video-24-bataljonu-Ajdar-1.png" alt="" width="1919" height="1079" srcset="https://euromaidanpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/24-oshb-Ajdar-ta-33-OSHP-v-Malyh-shherbakah-12.10.2025.-Stop-kadr-z-video-24-bataljonu-Ajdar-1.png 1919w, https://euromaidanpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/24-oshb-Ajdar-ta-33-OSHP-v-Malyh-shherbakah-12.10.2025.-Stop-kadr-z-video-24-bataljonu-Ajdar-1-300x169.png 300w, https://euromaidanpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/24-oshb-Ajdar-ta-33-OSHP-v-Malyh-shherbakah-12.10.2025.-Stop-kadr-z-video-24-bataljonu-Ajdar-1-1024x576.png 1024w, https://euromaidanpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/24-oshb-Ajdar-ta-33-OSHP-v-Malyh-shherbakah-12.10.2025.-Stop-kadr-z-video-24-bataljonu-Ajdar-1-1536x864.png 1536w, https://euromaidanpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/24-oshb-Ajdar-ta-33-OSHP-v-Malyh-shherbakah-12.10.2025.-Stop-kadr-z-video-24-bataljonu-Ajdar-1-380x214.png 380w, https://euromaidanpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/24-oshb-Ajdar-ta-33-OSHP-v-Malyh-shherbakah-12.10.2025.-Stop-kadr-z-video-24-bataljonu-Ajdar-1-800x450.png 800w, https://euromaidanpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/24-oshb-Ajdar-ta-33-OSHP-v-Malyh-shherbakah-12.10.2025.-Stop-kadr-z-video-24-bataljonu-Ajdar-1-1160x652.png 1160w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 1919px) 100vw, 1919px" /></a><figcaption id="caption-attachment-366194" class="wp-caption-text">Soldiers of the 24th Aidar Battalion and the 33rd Separate Assault Regiment in Mali Shcherbaky, 12 October 2025. Frame from a video by the 24th Aidar Battalion.</figcaption></figure>
<h3 id="recent-occupation">Recent occupation</h3><div data-fuse="incontent_2"></div>
<p>According to monitoring service DeepState, Russian troops had captured the village of Pyatykhatky and reached the outskirts of Shcherbaky, Mali Shcherbaky, and Stepove in March 2025. This initial push had allowed Russia to advance up to 4 kilometers deep along a 10-kilometer stretch.</p>
<p>Russian forces were later <a href="https://militarnyi.com/uk/news/bijtsi-gur-ta-girski-pihotyntsi-vidbyly-shherbaky-na-zaporizhzhi-ta-polonyly-okupantiv/">expelled from Shcherbaky by combined efforts of the 128th Mountain Assault Brigade and Ukraine’s military intelligence</a> agency, the HUR. However, Moscow struck again in July. Due to pressure on the western flank near the village of Kamianske, Russian forces seized Lobkove, Stepove, and part of Mali Shcherbaky.</p>


<p></p>


          <div class="read-also">
          <div class="read-also__inner">
