		<enclosure url="https://euromaidanpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/mali-shcherbaky-on-ukraine-map-flag-1024x492.jpg" length="113213" type="image/jpeg" />	</item>
		<item>
		<title>Up to 25,000 Cubans may be lured in Russia&#8217;s war by pay, but Havana emphasizes it has no connection to foreign recruitment for Moscow</title>
		<link>https://euromaidanpress.com/2025/10/12/up-to-25000-cubans-may-be-lured-in-russias-war-by-pay-but-havana-emphasizes-it-has-no-connection-to-foreign-recruitment-for-moscow/</link>
		
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[Olena Mukhina]]></dc:creator>
		<pubDate>Sun, 12 Oct 2025 16:13:38 +0000</pubDate>
				<category><![CDATA[Latest news Ukraine]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[armed conflict]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[baseless accusations]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Cuba]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Cuban involvement]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Cuban MFA]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[financial aid.]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Havana]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[international relations]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[mercenaries]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Moscow]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[political support]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Russia]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Russia’s war against Ukraine]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[U.S. accusations]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[US]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[war in Ukraine]]></category>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">https://euromaidanpress.com/?p=366161</guid>

					<description><![CDATA[The Cuban Foreign Ministry calls the accusations baseless and slanderous. ]]></description>
										<content:encoded><![CDATA[<p><img width="528" height="330" src="https://euromaidanpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/05/F73la_oWYAAXQiU.jpg" class="attachment-large size-large wp-post-image" alt="ukrainian intel nearly 20000 cuban mercenaries fighting russia’s side against ukraine nationals wearing russian military uniform 2023 video x/pstyle0ne1 florida lawmakers officials highlighted threat regional security news reports" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="https://euromaidanpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/05/F73la_oWYAAXQiU.jpg 528w, https://euromaidanpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/05/F73la_oWYAAXQiU-300x188.jpg 300w, https://euromaidanpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/05/F73la_oWYAAXQiU-380x238.jpg 380w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 528px) 100vw, 528px" /></p><div data-type="_mgwidget" data-widget-id="1845881"></div>        
        <script>
            (function(w,q){w[q]=w[q]||[];w[q].push(["_mgc.load"])})(window,"_mgq");
        </script>
    <p>The <strong>Cuban Ministry of Foreign Affairs</strong> firmly rejects the US government's claims that Cubans are participating in Russia’s war against Ukraine. In a statement published on <b>11 October</b>, it called these accusations <strong>baseless and “slanderous.”</strong></p>
<div class="pk-content-block pk-block-bg pk-block-bg-light">During the Soviet era, <strong>Cuba was a key Kremlin ally</strong>, and the friendship with Moscow continues today. <span style="margin-top: 0px;margin-right: 0px;margin-left: 0px;padding: 0px">Current relations are maintained through <strong><a target="_blank" href="https://www.radiosvoboda.org/a/skhemy-kuba-rosiya-naymantsi/33311322.html" rel="noopener">supplies</a> of petroleum products and food</strong>, as well as <strong>financial and political support</strong> for the Cuban government, according to Radio Free Europe/Radio Liberty</span>.</div>
<p>It also<strong><a target="_blank" href="https://cubaminrex.cu/en/cuba-categorically-rejects-claims-participation-conflict-ukraine" rel="noopener"> emphasizes</a> that Cuba is not participating in the war</strong>, nor does it deploy military personnel to any other country.</p>
<p><strong>Earlier, the Ukrainian Intelligence <a target="_blank" href="https://euromaidanpress.com/2025/09/18/ukrainian-intel-nearly-20000-cuban-mercenaries-fighting-on-russias-side-against-ukraine/" rel="noopener">said</a> that Cuban fighters form the second-largest foreign mercenary group in Russia’s ranks.</strong></p><div data-fuse="incontent_1"></div>
<hr>
<h3 id="individual-motives-vs-government-position"><strong>Individual motives vs. government position</strong></h3>
<p>In October 2025, <strong>Forbes <a target="_blank" href="https://www.forbes.com/sites/davidkirichenko/2025/10/07/cubans-could-soon-become-russias-largest-foreign-fighting-force/" rel="noopener">reported</a></strong> that up to <strong>25,000 Cubans could potentially join the war</strong> for financial rewards — around <strong>$2,000 per month</strong>, far above the average salary in Cuba.</p>
<p>The ministry stressed that <strong>no Cuban acts with the support or consent of the state</strong>. Recruitment occurs through <strong>foreign organizations, mostly abroad, without any connection to the Cuban government</strong>.</p>
<div class="pk-content-block pk-block-bg pk-block-bg-light">Amid the ongoing Russo-Ukrainian war, Moscow continues to suffer heavy losses of military personnel. Unwilling to announce a new wave of mobilization, the Kremlin turns to contract soldiers, including foreign nationals, to <strong>fill the gaps</strong>. Ukraine’s Main Intelligence Directorate <a target="_blank" href="https://euromaidanpress.com/2025/09/18/ukrainian-intel-nearly-20000-cuban-mercenaries-fighting-on-russias-side-against-ukraine/" rel="noopener">says</a> Moscow's intelligence services travel worldwide to recruit foreign fighters.</div>
<p>Cuban authorities maintain a <strong>zero-tolerance policy toward mercenarism and citizens’ participation in foreign conflicts</strong>.</p><div data-fuse="incontent_2"></div>
<h3 id="baseless-and-mendacious-accusations">"Baseless and mendacious accusations"</h3>
<blockquote>
<p class="text-align-justify"><em>"The Cuban Government categorically reaffirms that Cuba is not part of the armed conflict in Ukraine, nor does it participate with military personnel there or in any other country,"</em> the ministry said. </p>
</blockquote>
<p>Cuban diplomats also emphasized that the <strong>US government has provided no evidence</strong> to support its claims. It dubbed these accusations part of a discrediting campaign against Cuba that lacks a factual basis.</p>
<p>Meanwhile, the Ukrainian Intelligence representatives claim that Cuban mercenaries not only fight in Russia's war, but the country itself is a link in Moscow's network built to<strong> bypass sanctions, together with China, Iran, and North Korea</strong>.</p>
<p>According to intelligence data, critical microchips and other components flow into Russia’s defense industry through these countries. Officials stated that 60% of Russia’s artillery shells come from North Korea, while Iranian drones are used in major strikes against Ukrainian infrastructure. </p>

          <div class="read-also">
          <div class="read-also__inner">
                          <h2 id="read-also" class="read-also__headline">
                Read also              </h2>
                        
            <ul class="read-also__list">
                        
                                  <li>
                                        
                                        
                      <a href="https://euromaidanpress.com/2024/05/13/forbes-russia-hires-mercenaries-against-ukraine-in-at-least-21-countries/" target="_blank" class="read-also__title">
                        <h3 id="forbes-russia-hires-mercenaries-against-ukraine-in-at-least-21-countries">Forbes: Russia hires mercenaries against Ukraine in at least 21 countries</h3>
                      </a>
                                      </li>
                  
                        
                  
                          </ul>
          </div>
      </div>
    


<p></p>

