        </script>
    ]]></content:encoded>
					
		
		
			</item>
		<item>
		<title>Ukraine backs Italian Olympic ceasefire proposal, while recalling Russia&#8217;s history of wartime truce violations</title>
		<link>https://euromaidanpress.com/2025/10/11/ukraine-backs-italian-olympic-ceasefire-proposal-while-recalling-russias-history-of-wartime-truce-violations/</link>
		
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[Vira Kravchuk]]></dc:creator>
		<pubDate>Sat, 11 Oct 2025 11:19:52 +0000</pubDate>
				<category><![CDATA[Latest news Ukraine]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[ceasefire Olympics]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Milan-Cortina Winter Olympics]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Olympics]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Ukrainian Foreign Ministry]]></category>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">https://euromaidanpress.com/?p=366021</guid>

					<description><![CDATA[A Ukrainian Foreign Ministry official stated the country is prepared to halt hostilities now rather than waiting for the 2026 Winter Olympics, though they support Italian initiative aimed at stimulating Russia toward peace talks.]]></description>
										<content:encoded><![CDATA[<p><img width="959" height="606" src="https://euromaidanpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/07/Bloody-Olympics-protest-paris.jpg" class="attachment-large size-large wp-post-image" alt="Bloody Olympics Paris Russia" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="https://euromaidanpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/07/Bloody-Olympics-protest-paris.jpg 959w, https://euromaidanpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/07/Bloody-Olympics-protest-paris-300x190.jpg 300w, https://euromaidanpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/07/Bloody-Olympics-protest-paris-380x240.jpg 380w, https://euromaidanpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/07/Bloody-Olympics-protest-paris-800x506.jpg 800w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 959px) 100vw, 959px" /></p><div data-type="_mgwidget" data-widget-id="1845881"></div>        
        <script>
            (function(w,q){w[q]=w[q]||[];w[q].push(["_mgc.load"])})(window,"_mgq");
        </script>
    <p>Ukraine supports the proposal by Italian Foreign Minister Antonio Tajani to establish a <strong>ceasefire</strong> during the <strong>Winter Olympic Games,</strong> which will take place in February 2026.</p>
<div class="pk-content-block pk-block-shadows">Russian athletes can compete at the 2026 Winter Olympics only as <strong>neutral independent</strong> participants, without their national flag, anthem, or team designation. The International Olympic Committee maintained these sanctions following Russia's 2022 full-scale invasion of Ukraine and the subsequent suspension of the Russian Olympic Committee in October 2023.<br><br>However, in September, the International <strong>Paralympic</strong> Committee <a href="https://euromaidanpress.com/2025/09/27/paralympics-restores-russia-and-belarus-full-membership-rights-suspended-since-2022-invasion/">lifted</a> partial suspensions of Russia and Belarus, <strong>restoring</strong> their full membership rights and opening the possibility for athletes to <strong>compete under national flags</strong> at future Paralympic Games.</div>
<p>Ukrainian Foreign Ministry spokesperson Heorhiy Tykhyi announced the position during a Friday briefing in Kyiv, according to <a href="https://interfax.com.ua/news/general/1111505.html">Interfax-Ukraine.</a></p>
<p>While welcoming Italian Foreign Minister Antonio Tajani's initiative, he pointed to an uncomfortable pattern: Russia has previously launched invasions of both Georgia and Ukraine <strong>during Olympic truces.</strong></p><div data-fuse="incontent_1"></div>
<p>The timing wasn't accidental, according to Tykhyi. Global media attention fixes on sporting competitions, providing cover for military operations.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>"Crimes can be committed against the backdrop of these events," he said.</p>
</blockquote>
<p class="whitespace-normal break-words">At the same time, Tykhyi emphasized that "Ukraine is ready for a ceasefire with Russia, without necessarily waiting for the Olympics."</p>
<p class="whitespace-normal break-words">"We are ready right now," the Foreign Ministry stated.</p>
<p>Russia has continued to disregard ceasefire proposals from the United States, Tykhyi noted. Yet he suggested Ukraine would accept an Olympic-timed truce if that proves the only framework Moscow will consider.</p><div data-fuse="incontent_2"></div>
<blockquote>
<p>"If Russia needs an 'Olympic truce' for this, then let it be an 'Olympic truce.' But we insist that this happen sooner."</p>
</blockquote>
<p>The Italian proposal emerged ahead of the Milan-Cortina Winter Olympics, scheduled for 6-26 February 2026.</p>
<p>Tajani, who serves as both Deputy Prime Minister and Foreign Minister, submitted the plan to the United Nations calling for an Olympic truce covering all ongoing conflicts, specifically naming Ukraine and the Middle East.</p>
<p>Approximately<strong> 591 Ukrainian athletes and coaches have been killed</strong> since Russia's 2022 invasion.</p>
<p> </p>

